Add missing package markers for the Pallas lax lowerings.

JAX 0.10.2 contains `jax/_src/lax/pallas_lowerings` and its `gpu`
subdirectory, but neither directory has an `__init__.py` file. Since JAX
uses `setuptools.find_packages()` during installation, these directories
are omitted from the installed Python package.

This causes runtime failures such as:

`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'jax._src.lax.pallas_lowerings'`

when code paths such as GPU `ragged_dot` lowerings try to import them.

Add `__init__.py` files to both directories so they are included in the
installed JAX package.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
diff --git a/jax/_src/lax/pallas_lowerings/__init__.py b/jax/_src/lax/pallas_lowerings/__init__.py
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/jax/_src/lax/pallas_lowerings/__init__.py
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+"""Pallas lowerings for lax primitives."""
diff --git a/jax/_src/lax/pallas_lowerings/gpu/__init__.py b/jax/_src/lax/pallas_lowerings/gpu/__init__.py
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/jax/_src/lax/pallas_lowerings/gpu/__init__.py
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+"""GPU Pallas lowerings for lax primitives."""
